That makes SpaceX a controlled company

292
00:10:51,488 --> 00:10:53,639
under Nasdaq rules.

293
00:10:53,883 --> 00:10:56,463
The prospectus is blunt about it.

294
00:10:56,463 --> 00:10:59,146
It says the company is highly dependent

295
00:10:59,146 --> 00:11:00,073
on Mr.

296
00:11:00,073 --> 00:11:00,493
Musk,

297
00:11:00,493 --> 00:11:02,483
that it does not carry key person

298
00:11:02,483 --> 00:11:04,008
life insurance on him,

299
00:11:04,008 --> 00:11:05,777
and that he does not devote his

300
00:11:05,777 --> 00:11:07,081
full time to SpaceX,

301
00:11:07,081 --> 00:11:09,449
because he also runs Tesla.

302
00:11:09,683 --> 00:11:12,993
The second big dependence is government.

303
00:11:13,233 --> 00:11:14,432
One customer,

304
00:11:14,432 --> 00:11:16,365
which the filing does not name,

305
00:11:16,365 --> 00:11:19,056
accounted for about twenty-one percent of

306
00:11:19,056 --> 00:11:22,103
SpaceX's revenue in twenty twenty-five.

307
00:11:22,393 --> 00:11:24,651
Its government contracts are mainly with

308
00:11:24,651 --> 00:11:25,306
NASA,

309
00:11:25,306 --> 00:11:26,865
the Department of War,

310
00:11:26,865 --> 00:11:29,801
the General Services Administration and

311
00:11:29,801 --> 00:11:31,982
intelligence agencies.

312
00:11:32,217 --> 00:11:34,977
Let me draw the control panel.

313
00:11:35,057 --> 00:11:36,136
Here is SpaceX,

314
00:11:36,136 --> 00:11:38,177
with its three businesses.

315
00:11:38,177 --> 00:11:40,370
Here are the ordinary shareholders,

316
00:11:40,370 --> 00:11:41,707
with their shares.

317
00:11:41,767 --> 00:11:43,231
And here is one person,

318
00:11:43,231 --> 00:11:45,353
holding more than eighty percent of the

319
00:11:45,353 --> 00:11:46,377
votes.

320
00:11:46,517 --> 00:11:49,677
Every arrow of control runs through one

321
00:11:49,677 --> 00:11:50,564
box.

322
00:11:50,817 --> 00:11:54,267
So how does SpaceX actually make money?

323
00:11:54,267 --> 00:11:56,457
Not mainly from rockets.

324
00:11:56,617 --> 00:11:59,370
The rocket business has been losing money,

325
00:11:59,370 --> 00:12:01,717
because SpaceX is pouring billions into

326
00:12:01,717 --> 00:12:02,336
Starship,

327
00:12:02,336 --> 00:12:04,043
and most launches carry its own

328
00:12:04,043 --> 00:12:05,497
satellites.

329
00:12:05,617 --> 00:12:08,227
Starlink makes the operating profit.

330
00:12:08,227 --> 00:12:10,112
And now the biggest revenue line is

331
00:12:10,112 --> 00:12:11,977
artificial intelligence,

332
00:12:11,977 --> 00:12:14,071
much of it from renting out computing

333
00:12:14,071 --> 00:12:14,679
power,

334
00:12:14,679 --> 00:12:16,983
with one unnamed customer bringing in

335
00:12:16,983 --> 00:12:19,078
about a third of the latest quarter's

336
00:12:19,078 --> 00:12:20,097
revenue.

337
00:12:20,457 --> 00:12:22,069
The lesson is that the most famous

338
00:12:22,069 --> 00:12:23,860
part of a company is not always

339
00:12:23,860 --> 00:12:25,177
the part that pays.

340
00:12:25,317 --> 00:12:26,154
At SpaceX,

341
00:12:26,154 --> 00:12:28,493
the rocket is the delivery truck,

342
00:12:28,493 --> 00:12:30,403
Starlink is the cash register,

343
00:12:30,403 --> 00:12:32,764
and the newest business is a landlord

344
00:12:32,764 --> 00:12:34,437
with very large bills.

345
00:12:34,567 --> 00:12:36,952
Whether that mix keeps working depends on

346
00:12:36,952 --> 00:12:37,644
Starship,

347
00:12:37,644 --> 00:12:39,528
on a few big customers,

348
00:12:39,528 --> 00:12:41,082
and on one man.

349
00:12:41,317 --> 00:12:43,695
Next time on The Hidden Economics,

350
00:12:43,695 --> 00:12:46,532
we follow the money behind another hidden

351
00:12:46,532 --> 00:12:48,877
link of the world economy.

352
00:12:49,097 --> 00:12:51,591
This is The Hidden Economics.
